 "lead_in_rule": "an exception for a set whose nominal walk is not a rung (set.json lead_in 'start_v0.4'; STAGE2_75_PLAN.md A8 as amended by the owner's decision of 15 Nov, DECISION_LOG.md P34, after the first builds of the three sets; changed after a result): every item starts with the stand and start_v0.4, the start from standing straight into the 0.40 m/s walk, in place of start, one stride of nominal and the change to 0.40 m/s; the strides of the 0.40 m/s walk before a command, the seed slot, the planned seconds' rules and the judged windows are those of every other set (the start's own file ends with 2 strides of the 0.40 m/s walk after its steady point and the change's with 3, Stage 1's windows: counted from the steady point a command comes one stride earlier on such a set); another rung is reached from 0.40 m/s through the neighbouring rungs' changes, one stride of each rung on the way; the home pose of the track's LIPM frequency is read from the 0.40 m/s walk's file (every walk file of a set holds the body's one home pose); a condition that needs the nominal walk is not run.  Every record of such a set carries lead_in, and a table that prints its rows labels them (the summary's cells and lines, the kinematic check's record).  A set whose set.json and entries disagree is refused: lead_in 'start_v0.4' on a set that holds its nominal walk, or another lead_in on a set that holds start_v0.4 and the 0.40 m/s walk and no nominal walk",
